{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-local-shadow-ordering","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:local-shadow-ordering","kind":"definition","title":"Local shadow-price ordering $\\preceq_q$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-unstable-atom"],"tags":["ordering","shadow-price","open-neighborhood","continuity","phase-boundary"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidKnot.LocalShadowOrdering","text":"local-shadow-ordering.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/local-shadow-ordering.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:local-shadow-ordering\"></a><p><strong>Definition.</strong>\n<em>For two partitions <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda_1, \\lambda_2</code> with shadow prices <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">y_{\\lambda_1}(q), y_{\\lambda_2}(q) \\in R</code>, the <strong>local shadow-price ordering</strong> at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> is:</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\lambda_1 \\;\\preceq_q\\; \\lambda_2\n  \\;\\iff\\;\n  \\exists\\, U \\ni q\\;\\text{open such that}\\;\n  |y_{\\lambda_1}(q')| \\;\\leq\\; |y_{\\lambda_2}(q')|\n  \\;\\;\\forall q' \\in U.</code></pre>\n<p><em>We read this as: \"<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda_1</code> has at most the energy of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda_2</code> on a neighborhood of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>\".</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/local-shadow-ordering.md","heading":"Definition","number":"12.4.6"}
